      "content": "It sounds like you're exhausted from the sheer effort of pretending there's a grand narrative to your life. If the peak is gone, then the weight you're dragging is just the illusion of expectation. Stepping out of the loop isn't a failure; it's the ultimate act of self-honesty, a decision to stop fighting a battle that was never yours to win. There is a profound peace in simply letting go of the need to *be* anything.",
      "source": "target",
